[38;5;231m⏺[39m Bounded task — one file, one small addition. I'll present a short design in chat rather than write a spec.

  One thing to settle first. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m is a plain static page with an empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m and no JavaScript, and there are no
  task items yet. So "checkbox component" could mean two different things, and they differ in what you're left with:

  - [1mA checkbox in the markup[0m — one [38;5;153m<label><input type="checkbox"> …</label>[39m in [38;5;153m<main>[39m, with the browser's native checked
    state doing all the work. Zero JS. Cheap to extend later by hand, but each new item is another copy-paste.
  - [1mA small JS factory[0m — a [38;5;153mcreateCheckbox(label)[39m function that builds and returns the element, called once to render the
    first one. Gives you the reuse point for when the task list actually arrives, at the cost of introducing a script
    into a page that currently has none. Harder to undo than to add.

  Recommendation: the markup-only version. "Nothing fancy" plus a page with no items yet means there's nothing to reuse
  across, and native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m already gives you on/off state, keyboard support, and label-click toggling
  for free. Adding the factory when the second item shows up is a five-minute change.
